description:
src/worker/mod.rs resolve_adapter() (line ~2812) silently falls back to the claude-sonnet built-in when the configured adapter (config.agent.default) is not found in the dispatcher's loaded adapter map. This causes workers to dispatch beads with claude-sonnet — which uses 'unbuffer -p claude' and triggers the PTY escape-sequence transform failure — instead of failing with a clear error.

## Root cause

When a worker starts with --agent claude-code-glm-47, if the adapter file is not found or not loaded into the dispatcher, resolve_adapter falls through to:

  if let Some(adapter) = self.dispatcher.adapter("claude-sonnet") {
      tracing::warn!(..., "configured adapter not found, using fallback");
      return Ok(adapter.clone());
  }

The warn log is never surfaced to the user and the worker silently degrades.

## Fix

Remove the claude-sonnet fallback block (lines ~2819-2826). The function should be:

  fn resolve_adapter(&self) -> Result<crate::dispatch::AgentAdapter> {
      let adapter_name = &self.config.agent.default;
      self.dispatcher.adapter(adapter_name)
          .cloned()
          .ok_or_else(|| anyhow::anyhow!(
              "configured agent adapter '{}' not found — check ~/.needle/agents/{}.yaml or ~/.local/bin/claude-config/agents/{}/config.json exists",
              adapter_name, adapter_name, adapter_name
          ))
  }

The last-resort first-built-in block should also be removed (or kept only if the adapter_name is literally empty/unset, which config validation should prevent).

## Complete when
- resolve_adapter returns Err (not Ok(claude-sonnet)) when config.agent.default is not in dispatcher
- Existing test resolve_adapter_returns_builtin updated to expect Err when adapter not found
- cargo test passes (push to main and wait for needle-ci)
